{
 "slug": "css3_flexbox_container_align",
 "course": "css",
 "order": 174,
 "url": "/css/css3_flexbox_container_align.asp",
 "title": "CSS Flexbox Align",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "CSS Flexbox Align"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "CSS align-items Property"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The align-items property\naligns the flex items vertically (on the cross-axis)."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "This property can have one of the following values:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "normal (default)",
    "stretch",
    "center",
    "flex-start",
    "flex-end",
    "baseline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": ".flex-container {\n\n  display: flex;\n  height: 200px;\n\n  align-items: center;\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss3_flexbox_align-items_center"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": ".flex-container {\n\n  display: flex;\n  height: 200px;\n\n  align-items: flex-start;\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss3_flexbox_align-items_flex-start"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": ".flex-container {\n\n  display: flex;\n  height: 200px;\n\n  align-items: flex-end;\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss3_flexbox_align-items_flex-end"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": ".flex-container {\n\n  display: flex;\n  height: 200px;\n\n  align-items: stretch;\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss3_flexbox_align-items_stretch"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "CSS align-content Property"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The align-content property aligns\nthe flex lines. It only has effect when flex items wrap onto multiple lines."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "This property can have one of the following values:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "stretch (default)",
    "center",
    "flex-start",
    "flex-end",
    "space-between",
    "space-around",
    "space-evenly"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": ".flex-container {\n\n  display: flex;\n  height: 400px;\n\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n\n  align-content: center;\n\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss3_flexbox_align-content_center"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": ".flex-container {\n\n  display: flex;\n  height: 400px;\n\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n\n  align-content: space-between;\n\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss3_flexbox_align-content_space-between"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "True Centering With Flexbox"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The following example shows how to solve a common style problem: true centering."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "To achieve true centering, set both the justify-content and the align-items properties to\ncenter for the flex container, and the flex item will be perfectly centered\nboth horizontally and vertically:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "True Centering"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": ".flex-container {\n  display: flex;\n  height: 400px;\n  justify-content:\n  center;\n  align-items: center;\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss3_flexbox_perfect_center"
  }
 ]
}